+# Provenance notes: README smoke-test fixture and the public dataset split
+
+Metadata-only document. No benchmark task content (prompts, claims,
+trajectories, answers) was opened to produce it. Prepared in response to
+[scaleapi/mcp-atlas#84](https://github.com/scaleapi/mcp-atlas/issues/84).
+
+## The README smoke-test fixture
+
+The fixture is the "Smoke-test one task" example in `README.md`
+(prompt: "What is the first word of the file at /data/Barber Shop.csv?",
+enabled tools `["filesystem_read_text_file"]`, expected answer "Customer",
+sandbox image `ghcr.io/scaleapi/mcp-atlas:1.2.7`).
+
+Established facts (all verifiable from git objects):
+
+| Fact | Value |
+|------|-------|
+| Fixture introduced | commit `b8fffac`, 2025-12-17 ("improve readme for clarity, change to default gpt-5.1") |
+| Expected-answer line added | commit `c64799a`, 2026-07-04 (Release v2.0.0) |
+| Fixture text at pinned README blob `ab7fe6a09e2e90c2f6ccfc4799e3c4261b3126e2` (commit `f24ba3fb0bfa484c86acb28431fad6d7282455f9`, tree `e778a3323ad78e606a0dd3dcae7b4d39f5a61259`, 2026-08-03) | byte-identical to `README.md` at HEAD |
+| Fixture section sha256 (heading through the closing curl fence) | `792b13907089a327f72c5f43970ca15c3d9516e93cea2fc714d283884f6716e9` |
+| Stable task ID on the fixture | none (population uses 24-char TASK IDs; the fixture carries none) |
+| Dataset revision/release pin on the fixture | none |
+| Fixture-generation provenance statement | none exists in the repo |
+
+## The public dataset split
+
+- Dataset: `ScaleAI/MCP-Atlas` on Hugging Face — public, ungated, CC-BY-4.0,
+  single parquet file (`MCP-Atlas.parquet`), `train` split, ~500 tasks.
+  Columns include `TASK` (unique 24-char ID), `PROMPT`, `ENABLED_TOOLS`,
+  `GTFA_CLAIMS`, `TRAJECTORY`.
+- Point-in-time metadata (retrieved 2026-10-15): dataset sha
+  `8c563b55d7c967755f474299848049834d624617`, last modified
+  `2026-08-03T18:16:35Z`.
+- `run_eval.py` now loads the dataset with an explicit revision pin
+  (`DATASET_REVISION`), so the public split is versioned and reproducible
+  instead of floating.
+
+## Findings (metadata-only verdict)
+
+1. **Fixture-to-population relationship: NOT DETERMINABLE from public,
+   non-content-bearing artifacts.** The fixture carries no stable task ID and
+   no dataset revision pin; the repo contains no fixture-generation manifest,
+   task-ID roster, mapping, or attestation that could establish whether the
+   fixture is independently synthetic, derived from, or identical to a
+   released benchmark task. Establishing it would require either a
+   maintainer-provided manifest or opening task content, which this document
+   deliberately does not do.
+2. **No public, versioned, non-content-bearing provenance artifact exists in
+   this repo.** A filename/content scan for manifest/roster/attestation/
+   provenance terms returns zero hits.
+3. **No stable, versioned, non-content-bearing method exists for mapping the
+   historical ten-row public-preview exposure to stable task IDs and dataset
+   revision.** No preview rows, preview documentation, or preview mapping
+   appear in the repo, its git history, or the dataset card.
+
+## What would close the gap (request to maintainers)
+
+- A fixture-generation manifest that records, for each README fixture, either
+  a stable task ID + dataset revision, or an explicit "independently
+  synthetic" attestation.
+- A published, versioned task-ID roster per dataset release.
+- A versioned mapping artifact for the historical ten-row preview exposure.
+- Revision-pinned dataset references in code (started here with
+  `DATASET_REVISION` in `run_eval.py`).
+
+Until those exist, any provenance claim about the fixture is unverifiable
+from public metadata, and this document marks it as such.
